	(text_box "Clocks Per Pixel (CPP)\n\n00 = 2 ticks per pixel (HRES = 320)\n01 = 4 ticks per pixel (HRES = 160)\n10 = 8 ticks per pixel (HRES = 80) (invalid)\n11 = 16 ticks per pixel (HRES = 40) (invalid)\n\n\nBits Per Pixel (BPP)\n\n00 = 1 BPP\n01 = 2 BPP\n10 = 4 BPP\n11 = 8 BPP (hypothetical - needs 3/3/2 DtoA)\n\n\nPage Size\n\n00 = 8KB\n01 = 16KB (pass through A13)\n11 = 32KB (pass through A13..14)\n10 = invalid (pass through A14 only)\n\nXA13 = (!PageSize0 n A13) u (PageSize0 n PagedA13)\nXA14 = (!PageSize1 n A14) u (PageSize1 n PagedA14)\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.18 115.57 0)
		(size 52.07 58.42)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1da8b4a5-e4f6-497d-85ca-a7b05f804e2e")
	)
	(text_box "ControlRegisters Module persists configurable settings that can be written to and read from the host\n\nEach register is a pair of latch and tri-state buffer. The routing in-between each provides control signals to the GPU, the buffer allows the values to be read and the latch allows them to be stored\n\nEach register requires an enable signal to select and a read and write control signal.\n\nWhile the address mapping could be contained within the register, it is externalised to provide room to grow while reducing the number of gates required\nA plug-in module for each register already exists within my homebrew 6309 project, this can be reused in a practical build\n\nThe select logic permits up to 8 registers before the addressing must be cascaded (see ControlRegisterBankSelect)\n\nThe specific use of each register is documented on this sheet separately"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.18 55.88 0)
		(size 52.07 57.15)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "baa71d20-4ad2-49b1-8354-62c9ae8f8532")
	)
	(text_box "Row Repeat (RR)\n\n00 = 1 row 200LPF (no repeat)\n01 = 2 rows 100LPF\n10 = 4 rows 50LPF\n11 = 8 rows 25LPF\n\n\nDevice Identifier\n\n0 = Bitmap Memory\n1 = Tile Memory\n2 = Sprite Memory\n3 = Font Generator\n4 = Control Registers\n\n\nInterrupt Control\n\nVP!Int = Enable interrupt on viewport row enter\n!VPInt = Enable interrupt on viewport row exit\n!RPInt = Enable interrupt on non repeat horizontal Sync\n!HSInt = Enable interrupt on horizontal sync\n!VSInt = Enable interrupt on vertical sync"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.83 176.53 0)
		(size 58.42 50.8)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d28c4979-e4b3-4839-addf-eacdcff06040")
	)
